#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""qp: the laws of a project, from upstream code to an exported, reproducible proof (QuickProof's tool).

  qp new NAME URL [--ref REF]          scaffold projects/NAME, pinned to REF (default: the latest release tag)
  qp tree NAME [--orig] [--out DIR]    the code under test: upstream at COMMIT (+ PATCH) + the project's files
  qp fuzz NAME [H..] [-n RUNS]         native runs under ASan/UBSan, unmodified upstream and patched
  qp fuzz NAME [H..] --libfuzzer      (preview) each law as a coverage-guided libFuzzer target, unmodified upstream
  qp interp NAME [H..] [-n RUNS]       CompCert's reference interpreter (the semantics of the theorems)
  qp mutants NAME [H..] [-k K]         harness strength: K mutants of the code under test, which harness kills them
  qp lint NAME [H..]                   the VST lint alone (switch fall-off, bitfields, blockers in each law's cone)
  qp check NAME [H..]                  lint + fuzz + interp + mutants, written to projects/NAME/CHECK.md
  qp assemble NAME OUT [--reuse L]     the proof repository: code, harnesses, framework submodule, contracts
  qp verify REPO [--rev REV] [-v]      the acceptance check of a proof repository, from a fresh clone
                                       (docs/QP.md); --coqchk also runs Coq's checker
  qp export NAME REPO [--rev REV]      verify, then copy the proof into projects/NAME/proofs/LABEL/
  qp rebuild NAME LABEL                rebuild an exported proof from upstream and the workspace alone
  qp examples [NAME..]                 check the examples of examples/: each proof rebuilt from its files and
                                       checked by qp verify, with this framework (offline)
  qp import-fuzz NAME TARGET.c [opts]  a law from a libFuzzer target (docs/FUZZ-IMPORT.md); (preview) AFL++ or
                                       honggfuzz harnesses (--style), other entry points (--entry/--init/--cleanup)
  qp import-svcomp NAME TASK.yml [..]  (preview) a law from an SV-COMP task (docs/SVCOMP.md); --verdicts: the
                                       expected verdicts
  qp import-cbmc NAME PROOF_DIR [opts] (preview) a law from a CBMC proof harness (docs/IMPORT-CBMC.md)
  qp audit NAME [H..] [-v] [--md F]    the Clight audit of each law's cone: VST blockers (exit 1) and review items
  qp replay NAME LAW INPUT.. [--interp] an imported law on concrete inputs, natively or under CompCert's interpreter
  qp fidelity NAME [LAW..] --corpus D  imported laws vs the original targets built the upstream way (FIDELITY.md)

The workspace is the directory that holds projects/NAME/: --workspace DIR, else $QP_WORKSPACE, else the nearest
ancestor of the current directory that has a projects/ directory.  A project is projects/NAME/ with
  project.conf     UPSTREAM (git URL or path), COMMIT (full hash), LOGICAL (Coq root of src), FRAMEWORK (a
                   framework commit or tag; empty: the framework checkout qp belongs to), CODE (upstream paths the
                   proof needs; empty = all), PATCH (command run at the tree root; empty = none), BROKEN (laws
                   known to be false), MUTATE (more files for qp mutants)
  quickproof.conf  the framework's config (tools/clight.sh) for the library units; qp adds one harness unit per
                   harness/*.c
  harness/         the laws: *.c (the first comment says the claim), shared *.h
  env.c, env/LAW.c optional: the nondet_* distributions of native and interpreter runs (env/LAW.c: one law's)
  patch/           optional: the idiom patch (PATCH) and its equivalence test
  fuzz.conf        optional: import-fuzz defaults and the upstream build of the original targets (qp fidelity)
  notes.md         optional: sections (## Code, ## Not covered) for templates (qp assemble --templates)
  STATUS.md        laws and their status;  CHECK.md, FIDELITY.md  the last gate reports;  proofs/LABEL/  exports

The framework used for a project is its FRAMEWORK pin, taken from the git repository qp belongs to when it has
the commit, else from $QP_FRAMEWORK_URL (the public repository); $QP_FRAMEWORK_DIR overrides it (framework
development).  Machine settings: QP_* environment variables, or KEY=VALUE lines in $QP_SITE_CONF or
tools/site.conf (tools/site.conf.example).  Documentation: docs/QP.md.
"""
